Problem Statement: Household Electricity Cost Optimization using Grey Wolf Optimizer
The aim of this project is to optimize household electricity consumption by scheduling electrical appliances during time slots with lower electricity tariffs. 
Appliances such as air conditioners, washing machines and water heaters consume varying amounts of energy and contribute to the overall electricity bill. 
The system uses the Grey Wolf Optimizer (GWO) algorithm to find an optimal operating schedule for these appliances while satisfying their operating constraints.
The objective is to minimize the total electricity cost by intelligently allocating appliance usage across different time slots, thereby reducing household electricity expenses.
